[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-01-overview.png[/img]
[b]Build 0.9.15[/b]

RimWorld's Work tab tells you what you asked your colonists to do. It doesn't tell you what they actually did, who should be doing what, or which jobs are quietly never getting done.

[b]Human Resources[/b] is an HR manager for your colony. It watches how every colonist spends their time, works out who is best at what from more than raw skill level, spots the work that is falling behind and says why, and lets you run the whole colony from [b]job titles[/b] you design yourself.

No buildings, items or research. One [b]HR[/b] button on the bottom bar, one [b]Title[/b] column on the Work tab, and optional badges on the colonist bar.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/glance.png[/img]

[b]Required:[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]. RimWorld 1.7 only. No DLC needed.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-03-titles.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/titles.png[/img]

A job title is a named set of work priorities. Build "Doctor" once, stack it with "Crafter" and a default baseline, and reuse it in every colony.

[list]
[*][b]Set up like the Work tab:[/b] same order, same boxes, same clicks. Start from a colonist's priorities or copy another title.
[*][b]Edit once, update everyone[/b] who holds it.
[*][b]Up to five titles per colonist[/b], dragged into order. Each title is used as written; if two set the same work, the higher one wins. A coloured bar under each box shows which title set it.
[*][b]Default title:[/b] everyone gets it as their lowest title, new colonists too, and it doesn't use a slot.
[*][b]Hand edits are kept[/b] on top of titles, marked with a white frame and a * in the Title column.
[*][b]Reviews and Best suited:[/b] each holder gets a one-line review, and the three best candidates are listed.
[*][b]Library:[/b] save a title and load it in any other game.
[*][b]Title column:[/b] click a cell to change a colonist's titles, or the header to assign, add or remove titles for everyone.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-02-pages.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/pages.png[/img]

[b]Time use[/b] shows one stacked bar per colonist over the last 6 hours, 24 hours or 3 days: each kind of work, plus sleep, eating, recreation, idle, drafted, downed, mental breaks and walking. Click a category to hide it and recalculate; right-click to rank colonists by it.

Whoever you select in game is highlighted on every HR page, and picking a colonist in HR selects them in game.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-04-advice.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/job-advisor.png[/img]

[b]Workload[/b] tells you which work is keeping up and which is not, and why:

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/workload-statuses.png[/img]

[list]
[*]Each row has a 48-hour chart, who is on it, and [b]one suggestion[/b] that changes one named colonist, with its own Apply button.
[*][b]Show me where:[/b] click a kind of work to step the camera through each waiting item, with what looks wrong: forbidden, no path, in fog, nowhere to store it, or already claimed.
[*]"Leave out..." excludes a bill or workbench that only has work now and then.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-05-settings.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/options.png[/img]

[b]Mod support[/b]
[list]
[*][b][FSF] Complex Jobs:[/b] its split work types are tracked, advised and titled separately. Nurse is treated as unskilled care work and kept off Doctors and Surgeons.
[*][b]Vanilla Skills Expanded:[/b] expertise counts toward fit and is listed per colonist.
[*][b]Passion mods (Alpha Skills and similar):[/b] counted and shown, with the mod's own icon where it can be found.
[*][b]Mods adding work types:[/b] appear automatically on every page and in titles.
[/list]
None of these is required.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-06-faq.png[/img]
[b]Add to an existing save?[/b] Yes. Tracking starts when it is added, so Time use and Workload need a day or two of game time.

[b]Remove mid-save?[/b] Colonists keep their priorities. Expect a one-time error about the missing HR data. Not tested.

[b]Does it change priorities on its own?[/b] No, unless you turn on Daily review or Rest unused work.

[b]Performance?[/b] One sample per colonist per second, one count of waiting work per hour. The advisor only calculates while its page is open, or once a day with Daily review on.

[b]Two titles both use priority 1?[/b] Both stay at 1 and the game picks left to right. Set one to 2 to force an order.

[b]"Stuck bills" on a bill that's fine?[/b] It has nothing to do right now. Use "Leave out...".

[b]Expertise percentages?[/b] An estimate of how Vanilla Skills Expanded scales them.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-07-bugs.png[/img]
This build is running in one heavily modded colony but has had [b]no systematic testing[/b]. Expect rough edges. Report bugs with the version number from the mod list and your log.

